notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:22:07.149Z","harness:claude-code","Consequence measured 2026-07-29: the inverted child rows now produce a live validate warning, but under the wrong class name.\n\nState at measurement. pm validate reports validate_hierarchy_parent_cycle:1 with parent_cycle_item_count 8 and sample path pm-2xl->pm-j7a->pm-2xl. The eight named ids are pm-2xl, pm-54d, pm-b1w, pm-c0r, pm-f45, pm-j7a, pm-jiw, pm-u9r: the seven v1 milestone Epics plus the program root they all point at.\n\nWhy it appeared now and not before. The seven rows have carried created_at 2026-02-17T23:01:10Z and author steve since the v1 program was tracked. They were inert for five months because the scalar parent channel was empty on those Epics, so the two hierarchy channels never had to agree. On 2026-07-28 the scalar parent was set to pm-j7a on all seven to make the v1 origin reachable from a graph walk. That write was correct on its own channel. The pre-existing dependency rows assert the opposite direction on the same pair, so the combined hierarchy relation now contains a two-node cycle for every one of the seven.\n\nThe precise contradiction, on one pair. pm-2xl carries scalar parent pm-j7a, and simultaneously carries dependency row id pm-j7a, kind child. The registry declares child with hierarchyDirection source_parent, so that row asserts pm-2xl is the parent of pm-j7a. One item, two channels, opposite answers, both accepted at write time by the channel that received them.\n\nThe eight uninverted rows are the control. pm-7t04 holds five child rows to pm-0nia, pm-1265, pm-8rjn, pm-b8rf, pm-g2nd, and pm-v7dj holds three to pm-aqat, pm-jauk, pm-ze5g. All eight obey source_parent, none of the eight targets carries a contradicting scalar, and none of them appears in the cycle set. Direction alone separates the two groups; nothing else about the rows differs.\n\nWhat this changes about the item. Acceptance criterion three asked validate to report the dependency-row-versus-scalar-parent divergence as its own data-quality class with the offending ids named. Validate does now name all eight ids, but it names them under a cycle class. A cycle class tells a reader that the hierarchy is circular and invites the repair of breaking one arbitrary edge. The truth is that the hierarchy is a tree and one of the two encodings of the same edge is reversed, which has exactly one correct repair. The misclassification is therefore not cosmetic: it points remediation at the wrong operation. The divergence warning class stays required even though a warning now fires, and it should preempt the cycle class whenever every cycle edge in a component is a hierarchy pair whose two directions disagree.\n\nSecond measured consequence. graph audit is still unchanged at eleven info findings with no direction or cardinality finding among them, so the audit surface remains silent on a condition validate is loud about. pm-j7a now carries seven incoming child rows against a declared incoming cardinality of one, and nothing counts them.\n\nData repaired the same day, product defect retained. The seven inverted rows were removed so the tracker stops carrying a self-contradicting hierarchy; the scalar parent remains as the single surviving encoding and pm-j7a keeps its seventy descendants. All seven Epics carry release v2026.3.9, so the write is changelog-neutral. Removal is a data repair only. Nothing in the product prevents the next writer from recreating the identical contradiction, which is what this item still owns."
body: ""
